C1 End_{F_p}(E) != Z: deg(pi)=p, deg([m])=m^2; p prime is never a square
   primes p < 2e5 that are perfect squares: []  (expected [])
   toy E: p=15619 N=15761; pi(G)==G on E(F_p): True (pi acts as [1] on E(F_p), yet pi != [1] as an isogeny: deg p vs 1)
C2 endomorphism image oracle on a prime-order j=0 curve
   p=43651 N=43633 lam=30778 lam^2+lam+1 mod N = 0
   phi(Q)==[lam]Q for 50 random Q: True
   label-only simulator cost (double-and-add) = 21 group ops; bound 2*ceil(log2 N) = 32; literal 'm group operations' with m=lam would be ~30778
C3 incidence SEARCH (subset form) solves DLP in one query
   p=12487 N=12343 (14 bits): recovered k in 5/5 trials; adversary cost = 13 group ops + 1 SEARCH query (vs sqrt(N) ~ 111)
C4 incidence SEARCH, fixed arity m: exponent 1/(m+1) in queries+ops
